l that we think of a  business whereas the conscious business  is a self-adaptive holistic complex  system the best way though is that  recognize that traditional CSR is simply  grafting an artificial philosophy on  usually handled by the PR department in  most corporations why it's rightfully  called greenwashing because the  corporation is doing what it needs to do  to get favorable publicity but it  doesn't fundamentally care it hasn't  really transformed itself to make it  part of the DNA of the enterprise CSR  also generally tends to assume that all  good deeds are equally desirable and  I'll submit the conscious business is  attempting to make its social  responsibility environmental  responsibility part of its core mission  it's not and so that you have to you  focus on the on the social  responsibility in the environmental  that's consistent with everything else  that your business is doing that aligns  with it it's not an add-on let me push  down through just briefly talk a little  bit about not-for-profit organizations  because they have something to teach  business they get the thing about  purpose they are all motivated by a  deeper purpose that is the great lesson  that they had to teach the business  world today unfortunately they are not  able to transcend self-interest just  because they have a deeper purpose and  they oftentimes have sort of an  anti-business anti corporation and anti  profit mentality which holds them back  from reaching their fullest potential  therefore making them not as sustainable  as they could be over the long term in  fact they also  need to develop to a higher holistic  model and here's I've modeled out the  the conscious nonprofit organizational  model does that look familiar it's  exactly the same as the conscious  business the only difference is instead  of having a business mission it has a  social mission and instead of having  motivated investors it has motivated  donors otherwise the model is very very  similar and 